steps.message:
The project builds successfully. (The working tree shows no `git diff` because this checkout lives under a path ignored by the enclosing repo's `.gitignore`, so here is the patch explicitly.)

## Root cause

`favorites-hide` ("Hide favorites bar initially") hides the favorites bar via `ExperienceTweaks.updateSearchRecords()` whenever the query is empty. The **only** code that could make it visible again lived inside `doAction("display-history")`, and that action is only triggered by a tap when the *separate* `history-onclick` preference is enabled (or when the user re-mapped an up/down fling to `display-history` — the gesture-customisation feature introduced in the release the reporter updated to).

Since `preferences.xml` makes `favorites-hide` depend only on `history-hide` (Minimalistic UI), the exact repro settings (favorites above search bar + Minimalistic UI + Hide favorites bar initially) leave the bar hidden at startup with **no way to ever reveal it** — tapping the screen does nothing. Revealing the favorites bar was wrongly coupled to the history/gesture action logic.

## Patch

`app/src/main/java/fr/neamar/kiss/forwarder/ExperienceTweaks.java`

```diff
@@ case "display-history": (inside the GestureDetector's doAction)
                         }

-                        if (isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()) {
-                            mainActivity.favoritesBar.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
-                        }
+                        displayFavoritesBar();
                         break;
@@
     void onTouch(MotionEvent event) {
+        // When the favorites bar is initially hidden ("Hide favorites bar initially" setting),
+        // touching the home screen must always bring it back.
+        // This must not depend on other settings (such as displaying history on click,
+        // or having a gesture mapped to the "display history" action),
+        // otherwise the favorites bar could never be displayed again.
+        if (event.getActionMasked() == MotionEvent.ACTION_DOWN && mainActivity.isViewingSearchResults()) {
+            displayFavoritesBar();
+        }
+
         // Forward touch events to the gesture detector
         gd.onTouchEvent(event);
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Display the favorites bar if it's currently hidden
+     * because of the "hide favorites bar initially" setting
+     */
+    private void displayFavoritesBar() {
+        if (isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()) {
+            mainActivity.favoritesBar.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE);
+        }
+    }
```

## Why this fixes it and preserves behaviour

- Touching anywhere on the home screen (the touch listeners registered on `android.R.id.content` and the empty list view) now reveals the hidden favorites bar, restoring the reporter's previous behaviour — independent of `history-onclick`, `double-tap`, and gesture mappings.
- The reveal is gated on `isMinimalisticModeEnabledForFavorites()` (`history-hide` && `favorites-hide` && `enable-favorites-bar`), so nothing changes for users who don't use "Hide favorites bar initially".
- Gated on `isViewingSearchResults()` so the external bar isn't revealed underneath the all-apps KISS bar (where `Favorites.onDataSetChanged()` deliberately hides it).
- The existing hide paths are untouched: still hidden on startup/empty query (`ExperienceTweaks.updateSearchRecords`), when searching (`Favorites.updateSearchRecords`), and when the KISS bar closes (`onDisplayKissBar`).
- `display-history` (tap with `history-onclick`, or a fling mapped to it) behaves exactly as before — it now calls the extracted `displayFavoritesBar()` helper.

